    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d105">

                <pb facs="0186" n="179" sameAs="frus:frus1894Nicaragua/pg179"/>

                <head>No. 105.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-09-02"><hi rendition="#italic">September 2,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>After three days’ delay in acknowledging my communication delivered under your
                    instructions, by cable, August 29, the Government of Nicaragua refuses to accede
                    to your demand that prisoners be given trial. They contend that they are not
                    bound to give them trial by either the treaty of 1867 or by the laws of
                    Nicaragua. * * *</p>
                <p>Our next mail will reach Washington, D. C., October 4.</p>
            </div>
